//! The type-checking adapter of ai-ptc: the engine's `TypeChecker` port, with tsgo and the
//! checker's own rules (`archi/04-tools.md`, "Type-checking").
//!
//! [`TsgoChecker`] type-checks a script in strict mode against what the sandbox has, and
//! nothing else:
//!
//! | Declarations | From |
//! | --- | --- |
//! | ECMAScript lib, sandbox globals, the `ptc` module, `fetch` with the `http` tool | the sandbox lib of `crates/ptc-runtime/lib/`, embedded by path |
//! | `ptc:tools` | the toolset's `ptc-tools.d.ts`, generated by `ptc-codegen` |
//!
//! tsgo, the native TypeScript 7 compiler, has no programmatic API: it is driven as a CLI. Its
//! npm package for the target platform is embedded in the binary (see `build.rs`) and
//! extracted to a cache directory at first use. The checker's own rules (floating promises,
//! ignored async callbacks, absent globals) run on the swc syntax tree, and their diagnostics
//! join tsgo's.

#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

mod checker;
mod error;
mod rules;
mod sandbox;
mod source;
mod tsgo;

pub use checker::{HTTP_TOOL_REFERENCE, TsgoChecker};
pub use error::CheckError;
pub use tsgo::TSGO_VERSION;
